# the argument of spinoza-ethics-3.md as claude-opus-5-5 read it: check that it says what the text says
# Spinoza, note on the kinds of emotions: the side argument that luxury etc. have no contraries (S3-S4), and the main point that no further taxonomy is needed (S5-S8).
atom	immoderate_love	by luxury, drunkenness, lust, avarice, ambition we simply mean the immoderate love of feasting, drinking, venery, riches, and fame
atom	species_of_desire	luxury, drunkenness, lust, avarice, and ambition are merely species of love or desire
atom	temperance_not_emotion	temperance, sobriety, and chastity are not emotions or passive states, but indicate a power of the mind which moderates those emotions
atom	opposed_to_luxury	temperance, sobriety, and chastity are what we are wont to oppose to luxury, drunkenness, and lust
atom	no_contraries	these emotions, in so far as distinguished merely by their objects, have no contraries
atom	kinds_numerous	the kinds of emotions are as numerous as the kinds of objects
atom	cannot_explain	the remaining kinds of emotions cannot be explained here
atom	general_def_sufficient	a general definition of each emotion, and understanding the general properties of the emotions and the mind, is sufficient to determine the strength of the emotions and the mind's power over them
atom	great_difference	there is a great difference between various emotions of love, hatred, or desire
atom	no_need_differences	there is no need to take cognizance of such differences or to track out further the nature and origin of the emotions
P1	S2	immoderate_love	kind conceptual
C1	S1	species_of_desire	from P1
P2	S4	temperance_not_emotion
P3	S4	opposed_to_luxury	kind empirical
# The "For" in S4 relies on this link from the opposed virtues not being emotions to there being no contrary emotions.
A1	-	opposed_to_luxury ∧ temperance_not_emotion → no_contraries
C2	S3	no_contraries	from P2 P3 A1
P4	S5	kinds_numerous
P5	S5	kinds_numerous → cannot_explain
C3	S5	cannot_explain	from P4 P5
# S6 and S7 state the same sufficiency claim ("I repeat").
P6	S6	general_def_sufficient
P7	S7	general_def_sufficient
P8	S8	great_difference
# S8's "Thus" relies on sufficiency removing the need to track differences.
A2	-	general_def_sufficient → no_need_differences
C	S8	no_need_differences	from P6 A2
